uring startup.\\n\\nThe logs consistently end with:\\n\\n```text\\n[FATAL:content\\\\browser\\\\gpu\\\\gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc:415]\\nGPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.\\n```\\n\\nSignal additionally reports repeated GPU process failures before aborting:\\n\\n```text\\nGPU process exited unexpectedly: exit_code=-2147483645\\n```\\n\\nWindows Event Viewer records Application Error (Event ID 1000) with exception code:\\n\\n```\\n0x80000003\\n```\\n\\nThe faulting module is the application executable itself (e.g. `Obsidian.exe`, `Signal.exe`).\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nLaunching Obsidian normally:\\n\\n```powershell\\n& \\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\<user>\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Programs\\\\Obsidian\\\\Obsidian.exe\\\"\\n```\\n\\nResults in:\\n\\n* application exits almost immediately\\n* log ends with `GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.`\\n\\nThe same behavior is observed with Signal Desktop and Discord.\\n\\n## Startup Flag Testing\\n\\n### `--in-process-gpu`\\n\\nLaunching with:\\n\\n```text\\n--in-process-gpu\\n```\\n\\nchanges the behavior:\\n\\n* the process no longer exits immediately\\n* however, the application window is not rendered correctly (GUI is missing / blank)\\n\\n### Four-flag combination\\n\\nLaunching with:\\n\\n```text\\n--disable-gpu\\n--disable-gpu-compositing\\n--disable-software-rasterizer\\n--in-process-gpu\\n```\\n\\nchanges the behavior further.\\n\\nIn Safe Mode, this combination allows the UI to render instead of immediately terminating.\\n\\nOutside Safe Mode, startup behavior changes, but rendering is still incomplete or absent.\\n\\nThe fact that `--in-process-gpu` consistently changes the failure mode suggests the issue is related to Chromium's GPU process initialization.\\n\\n## Diagnostics Already Performed\\n\\n* Updated AMD driver to latest available version\\n* `sfc /scannow`\\n* Windows Defender scan\\n* Malwarebytes scan\\n* HDR disabled\\n* Safe Mode testing\\n* AMD Radeon Software terminated\\n* DxDiag reports no display or DirectX problems\\n\\nNone of the above resolved the issue.\\n\\nIf there are additional Chromium or Electron logging flags that would help diagnose why the GPU process exits, I would be happy to collect and provide them.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nVisual Studio Code launches normally on the same machine.\\n\\nThis suggests the issue is not a complete Electron failure, but may depend on the Electron/Chromium version or GPU initialization path used by different applications.\",\n  \"form\": \"bug\",\n  \"labels_already_applied\": [\n   \"blocked/need-info ❌\",\n   \"bug :beetle:\",\n   \"platform/windows\"\n  ],\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"opened\": \"2026-07-03T10:57:47Z\"\n },\n \"form_fields\": {\n  \"electron_version\": \"Electron 39.8.3\",\n  \"os\": \"Windows\",\n  \"last_known_working\": null,\n  \"testcase_gist_url\": null\n },\n \"repro\": {\n  \"gist\": false,\n  \"other_repo_link\": false,\n  \"code_blocks\": 6\n },\n \"bot_already\": {\n  \"asked_for_supported_version\": true,\n  \"need_repro_label\": false\n },\n \"issues_linked_by_reporter\": [\n  51761,\n  52098\n ],\n \"component_hints\": [\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/gpu\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"gpu\",\n    \"gpu process\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": true\n  }\n ],\n \"redirect_hints\": {\n  \"upstream\": [\n   \"chromium\"\n  ]\n },\n \"similar_candidates\": [\n  {\n   \"number\": 52098,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-06-23\",\n   \"score\": 130.9,\n   \"title\": \"GPU/renderer process crashes with EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT (0x80000003) on Windows 11 25H2 (build 26200.8655) — sandbox init failure, regression after June 2026 cumulative update\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"radeon\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"x80000003\",\n    \"faulting\",\n    \"0x80000003\",\n    \"goodbye.\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"-2147483645\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": true,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior The GPU (and renderer) child process launches normally under the sandbox. ### Actual Behavior The GPU process is killed by EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT (0x80000003 / exit_code=-2147483645) immediately on launch, **before any GPU vendor DLL is loaded**. The browser process retries 6 times within ~0.3s and then self-terminates. Browser process log (captured with --enable-logging=stderr\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51761,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-24\",\n   \"score\": 128.4,\n   \"title\": \"[Bug] Electron apps crash with exit_code=-2147483645 (GPU process sandbox crash) when zombie SIDs exist in DACL\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"programs\",\n    \"repeated\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"powershell\",\n    \"goodbye.\",\n    \"startup.\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"-2147483645\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": true,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Electron applications should launch normally even if the directory contains unparseable or orphaned zombie SIDs, or gracefully handle the permission validation error without crashing the entire GPU process. ### Actual Behavior The GPU process crashes on startup with exit_code=-2147483645 and outputs \\\"FATAL:gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc: GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.\\\" \"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51770,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-25\",\n   \"score\": 110.0,\n   \"title\": \"Child processes crash at launch in base::i18n::InitializeICUFromDataFile (ICU init CHECK fails), exit 0x80000003, Windows 11 26200\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"dxdiag\",\n    \"initialization.\",\n    \"x80000003\",\n    \"0x80000003\",\n    \"goodbye.\",\n    \"-2147483645\",\n    \"usable.\",\n    \"logging\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Electron child processes (GPU, renderer, utility) initialize and the app launches normally, as it does for Chromium/Chrome and for older-Electron apps on the same machine. ### Actual Behavior On this machine, every Electron child process aborts at the very first step of startup — before GPU init, sandbox lockdown, or logging — inside ICU initialization. The browser process is\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51767,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-25\",\n   \"score\": 99.1,\n   \"title\": \"GPU process exited unexpectedly: exit_code=-2147483645\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"programs\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"-2147483645\",\n    \"usable.\",\n    \"unexpectedly\",\n    \"appdata\",\n    \"fatal\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Antigravioty desktop and thorim browser from mini install has to run ### Actual Behavior i was using antigravity and thorim browser wihtout problem for one day. than after a restart neither antigravity nor thorim browser run again. When i drag antigravity executable in the CMD i have this errors and the log attached [language_server.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/fi\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51557,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-08\",\n   \"score\": 63.8,\n   \"title\": \"macOS 26.3 (Tahoe) - IME candidate window not displaying in textarea\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"consistently\",\n    \"suggests\",\n    \"flags\",\n    \"rendered\",\n    \"testing\",\n    \"missing\",\n    \"reproduction\",\n    \"issue.\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior When typing Chinese (using IME input methods such as Pinyin) inside a textarea in an Electron application on macOS, the IME candidate window should: * Display correctly under or near the text cursor * Show full candidate list (not only pre-edit text / pinyin) * Follow the caret position accurately during typing * Behave consistently with native applications and Chrome browser\"\n  }\n ],\n \"similar_search\": \"BM25 over issue-corpus.jsonl, only issues opened before 2026-07-03T10:57:47Z\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOu